.TH tuappinfo n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuappinfo
.PP
Collect application / system information into a plain\-text report: Tcl/Tk versions, executable, platform, selected environment variables, search paths, loaded packages, and an optional list of explicitly tracked module files. Supports anonymisation of user / host / path data. Pure Tcl, no GUI \-\- the caller renders the returned text (e.g. in a Tk window or a log file).
.SS API
.CS
::tclutils::tuappinfo::trackTm    file
::tclutils::tuappinfo::buildReport ?-title str? ?-anonymize 0|1?
::tclutils::tuappinfo::writeLog    file ?-title str? ?-anonymize 0|1?
.CE
.IP \(bu
\fBtrackTm\fR — record a module file path so it appears under "Loaded TM Modules" (otherwise that section reads "(none tracked)").
.IP \(bu
\fBbuildReport\fR — return the full report as a single string. \fB\-anonymize 1\fR masks user/host names (stable hash), \fBHOME\fR/\fBTEMP\fR paths, and \fBPATH\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fBwriteLog\fR — write \fBbuildReport\fR to \fBfile\fR; returns the file path.
.CS
puts [::tclutils::tuappinfo::buildReport -title "MyApp 1.0"]
::tclutils::tuappinfo::writeLog /tmp/myapp-info.txt -title "MyApp 1.0" -anonymize 1
.CE
.SS Demo
.CS
tclsh examples/demo-tuappinfo.tcl
.CE
